   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(80,0,80);margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">Hello Phil! </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">In the 3PL model, all hits at random (guess) are estimated, can I fix any of them? </font></span></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"> </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">The problem is that in the dataset I&#39;m working with I have 189 respondents and 40 items, therefore there are more estimated parameters (160) for two dimensions than response patterns (153). To assure the analyses, according to Reckase, the parameter estimates should be smaller than the response patterns.</font></span></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"> </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I would like to</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"> reduce the parameters by fixing only a few hits at random (guess) and thus ensure the reduction guess of the estimated parameters, since I already have a few hits at zero estimated randomly.</span></font></span></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"> </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0.0001pt;margin-left:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">How can I solve this? In mirt is there any model or code that does it?</font></span></p><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;padding-top:10px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:0px;width:22px\"><div role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Ocultar conteúdo expandido\" style=\"background-color:rgb(241,241,241);border-top-width:1px;border-right-width:1px;border-bottom-width:1px;border-left-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(221,221,221);border-right-color:rgb(221,221,221);border-bottom-color:rgb(221,221,221);border-left-color:rgb(221,221,221);clear:both;line-height:6px;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;width:20px\"><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/I0X05dDxpDvv2rZpMXlrbmy24gZg77zu4Ql_7IKBPSrx-X15wEW4wTvVyc1P_o0T288Up2W6ABQRpBfIURT0ddk8oH5yQCA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/images/cleardot.gif\" style=\"background-image:url(https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/WqzxozzKp2UsMOyJ9TeAP8VyvxEGIRSYkd2LU-eoxi4elZdCQkJ7nJ0vRTgoEbLm9B7bXKhOhbxlE-EXjoZRMgzh_k2GMJ71=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ssl.gstatic.com/ui/v1/icons/mail/ellipsis.png);background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-color:initial;min-height:8px;opacity:0.3;width:20px;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:no-repeat no-repeat\"></div></div></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
