  {
   "id": "B-Nib225jL4J",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2014-01-22T14:03:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: Guess",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Edy,<div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 22, 2014 at 5:24 AM, Edy Coelho <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">edyceli...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(80,0,80)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">Hello Phil! </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">In the 3PL model, all hits at random (guess) are estimated, can I fix any of them? </font></span></p>\r\n<div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"> </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">The problem is that in the dataset I&#39;m working with I have 189 respondents and 40 items, therefore there are more estimated parameters (160) for two dimensions than response patterns (153). To assure the analyses, according to Reckase, the parameter estimates should be smaller than the response patterns.</font></span></p>\r\n</span></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>I would say it should be much smaller. For most ML estimation its recommended to have at 5 times the sample size per parameter estimated. Of course that&#39;s a general recommendation since it depends on the type of parameters estimated. For instance, in Rasch models you can have a substantially smaller sample size since all that is being estimated are intercepts, which are extremely stable to begin with. </div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">\r\n<div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"> </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I would like to</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"> reduce the parameters by fixing only a few hits at random (guess) and thus ensure the reduction guess of the estimated parameters, since I already have a few hits at zero estimated randomly.</span></font></p>\r\n</span></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>Change the itemtype&#39;s you want to &#39;2PL&#39; instead, and supply a vector of guess values for the &#39;guess =&#39; input. Both itemtype and guess should be vectors then with the lengths equal to the number of items. There is an early example of this in the ?mirt documentation with the LSAT7 dataset. </div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Phil</div><div><br></div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<span style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\"> </font></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\" face=\"georgia, serif\">How can I solve this? In mirt is there any model or code that does it?</font></span></p><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;outline:none;padding:10px 0px;width:22px\">\r\n<div style=\"background-color:rgb(241,241,241);border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221);clear:both;line-height:6px;outline:none;width:20px\"><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/I0X05dDxpDvv2rZpMXlrbmy24gZg77zu4Ql_7IKBPSrx-X15wEW4wTvVyc1P_o0T288Up2W6ABQRpBfIURT0ddk8oH5yQCA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/images/cleardot.gif\" style=\"background-image:url(https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4Pr9QlSavgRrq9Z2e9xIdvM0tknChd1d3dwHXzb4AxHH58w0Ke02qizRBkj-OCDGy4wP2RrG7OYjvK0G5jWJojcVQldSGVQLT8rI=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ssl.gstatic.com/ui/v1/icons/mail/ellipsis.png);min-height:8px;width:20px;background-repeat:no-repeat no-repeat\"></div>\r\n</div></span></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><p></p>-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;mirt-package&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-package...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476374155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw339aIfKzN4XdUM4Jo9_TQq\">https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out</a>.<br></font></span></blockquote><div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div>\r\n</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
